# Style and verification

Match existing C++17 style: small types, no extra dependencies, real names, no
commented-out code. Touch only files the task needs. Keep `export/bbox_ekf/`
standalone (hpp + cpp + its README; no sim headers, no Eigen).

## Structure

- Estimators: `src/estimator/`. Export copy: `export/bbox_ekf/`.
- Sim / types: `src/sim/`. GUI: `src/ui/`. Logs: `src/io/`. App: `src/app/`.
- Math: `src/math/` (`linalg.hpp`). Shared structs: `src/sim/types.hpp`.
- Checks: `tools/*_check.cpp`, `tools/check.bat`. Build: `build.bat` → `build/`.

Prefer extending a type or function over a parallel ad-hoc path. Update
`export/bbox_ekf/README.md` when the export API or defaults change.

## Test / bench every feature

Do not ship a behaviour change unmeasured. Add or extend a check, run it, report
the numbers in the reply (and in the commit body if they change defaults).

| Kind of change | Preferred check |
|---|---|
| Export EKF / LOS / range | `tools/export_ekf_check.cpp` → `build/export_ekf_check.exe` |
| Sim estimator / timing | `tools/check.bat` or `build\drone_chase_sim.exe auto --quick` |
| Focal feature (range, size, LOS) | Score that quantity; include off vs on when adding a knob |

If a default would regress the quiet/smooth case, leave it off and document
when to enable it. Do not invent prices, URLs, or metrics you did not run.
